Here they are. P004 is already solved, so these are for comparison only. Read them as **"try every allowed move, keep the best"**.

**DP:** `dp[i]` = fewest jumps to land on `i`. From each spot you've reached, try every jump and improve the target.

```
public int JumpDp(int[] nums)
{
    int n = nums.Length;
    var dp = new int[n];
    Array.Fill(dp, int.MaxValue);     // "not reached yet"
    dp[0] = 0;                        // you start at 0

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (dp[i] == int.MaxValue) continue;          // can't stand here
        for (int d = 1; d <= nums[i] && i + d < n; d++) // every allowed jump
            dp[i + d] = Math.Min(dp[i + d], dp[i] + 1);
    }
    return dp[n - 1];
}
```

**BFS:** visit indices in "waves": first everything 1 jump away, then 2 jumps, and so on. The first time a wave touches the end, that's the minimum.

```
public int JumpBfs(int[] nums)
{
    int n = nums.Length;
    var dist = new int[n];
    Array.Fill(dist, -1);             // -1 = not visited
    dist[0] = 0;
    var queue = new Queue<int>();
    queue.Enqueue(0);

    while (queue.Count > 0)
    {
        int i = queue.Dequeue();
        if (i == n - 1) return dist[i];              // first touch = fewest jumps
        for (int d = 1; d <= nums[i] && i + d < n; d++)
        {
            int j = i + d;
            if (dist[j] != -1) continue;             // an earlier wave got here
            dist[j] = dist[i] + 1;
            queue.Enqueue(j);
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

